hokku-installer (4.0.0~beta2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v4.0.0-beta2. The USB data port's role now follows the appliance's
    mode, so "Flash a screen" works on the appliance and a stranded unit still
    gets a serial console. Setup-mode reboots no longer wedge: PID 1 is kept
    from opening the gadget tty during shutdown, and the last-resort swapfile
    is actually installed.

 -- Dennis Fleurbaaij <mail@dennisfleurbaaij.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 20:15:00 +0000

hokku-installer (4.0.1~dev.14-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The USB data port's role now follows the appliance's mode. New shared
    usb-mode.sh sets it: peripheral (gadget serial console) for setup mode,
    host for hokku mode so "Flash a screen" can drive a frame. The wizard
    switches to host on the reboot out of setup; reset.sh and the WiFi
    watchdog switch back, so a stranded appliance regains its console.

 -- Dennis Fleurbaaij <mail@dennisfleurbaaij.com>  Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:04:22 -0500

hokku-installer (4.0.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First public beta of the 4.0 appliance line. Captive-portal first-boot setup
    wizard (WiFi, hostname, mDNS, SSH, timezone/country) on the "Hokku Setup" AP;
    hands off to hokku-server once setup completes. No functional change since
    dev.18 — version aligned to the 4.0.0-beta1 release.

 -- Dennis Fleurbaaij <mail@dennisfleurbaaij.com>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 03:16:33 +0000

